note Exercism-style exercise "eliuds-eggs": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/eliuds-eggs
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note eggcount is the number of 1 bits in the binary representation of n.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/eliuds-eggs
om2
fn eggcount n ulong to ulong
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
